.member-hermes {\n  border: 5px solid #0da6d6;\n}\n\n.member-iquest {\n  border: 5px solid cyan;\n}\n\n.member-tP {\n  border: 5px solid #ff9f00;\n}\n\n.member-acer {\n  border: 5px solid silver;\n}\n\n/* SVG animations */\n\n@keyframes shipWheelSpin {\n  from {transform: rotate(0deg);}\n  to {transform: rotate(360deg);}\n}\n\n@keyframes orbBreath {\n  0%, 100% {transform: scale(1);}\n  50% {transform: scale(1.2);}\n}\n\n@keyframes wrenchSwing {\n  from {transform: rotate(0deg);}\n  to {transform: rotate(-10deg);}\n}\n\n@keyframes wingFlap {\n  from {transform: translateY(0) rotate(0deg);}\n  to {transform: translateY(-5px) rotate(-5deg);}\n}\n\n@keyframes bracketsPulse {\n  0%, 100% {transform: scale(1);}\n  50% {transform: scale(1.05);}\n}\n\n@keyframes screenFlicker {\n  0%, 100% {opacity: 1;}\n  50% {opacity: 0.5;}\n}\n\n@keyframes paneFade {\n  from {opacity: 1;}\n  to {opacity: 0.5;}\n}\n```\n\n```svg\n<!-- Ross member icon -->\n<svg class=\"member-icon\" viewBox=\"0 0 100 100\">\n  <path id=\"shipWheel\" d=\"...\" fill=\"#fff\"/>\n  <animate xlink:href=\"#shipWheel\" attributeName=\"transform\" from=\"rotate(0,50,50)\" to=\"rotate(-360,50,50)\" dur=\"2000\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/>\n</svg>\n\n<!-- Claude member icon -->\n<svg class=\"member-icon\" viewBox=\"0 0 100 100\">\n  <circle id=\"orb\" cx=\"50\" cy=\"50\" r=\"30\"/>\n  <animate xlink:href=\"#orb\" attributeName=\"r\" from=\"30\" to=\"40\" dur=\"2000\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/>\n</svg>\n\n<!-- Wren member icon -->\n<svg class=\"member-icon\" viewBox=\"0 0 100 100\">\n  <path id=\"wrench\" d=\"...\" fill=\"#fff\"/>\n  <animate xlink:href=\"#wrench\" attributeName=\"transform\" from=\"rotate(0,50,50)\" to=\"rotate(-10,50,50)\" dur=\"1500\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/>\n</svg>\n\n<!-- Hermes member icon -->\n<svg class=\"member-icon\" viewBox=\"0 0 100 100\">\n  <rect id=\"wing\" x=\"40\" y=\"20\" width=\"20\" height=\"60\"/>\n  <animate xlink:href=\"#wing\" attributeName=\"y\" from=\"20\" to=\"10\" dur=\"1500\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/>\n</svg>\n\n<!-- iQuest member icon -->\n<svg class=\"member-icon\" viewBox=\"0 0 100 100\">\n  <rect id=\"bracket\" x=\"30\" y=\"30\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\"/>\n  <animate xlink:href=\"#bracket\" attributeName=\"width\" from=\"40\" to=\"45\" dur=\"2000\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/>\n</svg>\n\n<!-- TP member icon -->\n<svg class=\"member-icon\" viewBox=\"0 0 100 100\">\n  <rect id=\"screen\" x=\"20\" y=\"20\" width=\"60\" height=\"60\"/>\n  <animate xlink:href=\"#screen\" attributeName=\"opacity\" from=\"1\" to=\"0.5\" dur=\"2000\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/>\n</svg>\n\n<!-- Acer member icon -->\n<svg class=\"member-icon\" viewBox=\"0 0 100 100\">\n  <rect id=\"pane\" x=\"10\" y=\"10\" width=\"80\" height=\"80\"/>\n  <animate xlink:href=\"#pane\" attributeName=\"opacity\" from=\"1\" to=\"0.5\" dur=\"2000\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/>\n</svg>\n```\n\nReplace `d=\"...\"` with the actual path data for the ship wheel and wrench icons, and replace the placeholder attributes in the other SVG elements with their appropriate values. The keyframes animations are defined in CSS to be applied to these SVG elements.", "wall_s": 16.8, "ts": "2026-07-03T12:43:37Z"}
{"worker": "forge", "role": "code_drafter", "model": "hermes3:8b", "model_requested": "codellama:13b", "fallback_skipped": ["codellama:13b", "qwen2.5-coder", "qwen2.5:7b", "iquest-coder-cpu:40b"], "task": "In 2 lines: any one small improvement you would ship to Wren's evolution loop today?", "reply": "# In `world.wren`, modify the `evolve` method:\n\n```gdscript\nfunc evolve(population):\n    var new_population = []\n    for individual in population:\n        if random() < MUTATION_RATE:\n            var mutated = individual.mutate()\n            new_population.append(mutated)\n        else:\n            new_population.append(individual)\n    return new_population\n```\n\nThis small patch adds a `mutate()` method call to the mutation branch of the loop, ensuring that mutations are actually being applied as intended.", "wall_s": 7.5, "ts": "2026-07-03T12:47:27Z"}
{"worker": "forge", "role": "code_drafter", "model": "hermes3:8b", "model_requested": "codellama:13b", "fallback_skipped": ["codellama:13b", "qwen2.5-coder", "qwen2.5:7b", "iquest-coder-cpu:40b"], "task": "In 2 lines: any one small improvement you would ship to Wren's evolution loop today?", "reply": "# In `evolution.gd`:\n\nfunc _process(delta):\n    # Already checks for input and processes it\n    if Input.is_action_just_pressed(\"ui_accept\"):\n        evolve()\n\nfunc evolve():\n    # Evolve the creature based on fitness score\n    var new_creature = creature.duplicate()\n    new_creature.mutate()\n    \n    # Small improvement: Add a random chance to keep the current creature\n    if not randf() < MUTATION_RATE:\n        set_creature(new_creature)\n\n# In `creature.gd`:\n\nfunc mutate():\n    # Already mutates properties based on mutation rate\n    for part in $Body.get_children():\n        if randf() < PART_MUTATION_RATE:\n            part.mutate()\n    \n    # Small improvement: Randomly remove a body part\n    if randf() < REMOVE_PART_CHANCE:\n        var parts = $Body.get_children()\n        if not parts.is_empty():\n            var random_part = parts[randi()%parts.size()]\n            random_part.queue_free()\n\n# In `main.py`:\n\nMUTATION_RATE = 0.01\nPART_MUTATION_RATE = 0.1\nREMOVE_PART_CHANCE = 0.05\n\nThese changes introduce a small chance (REMOVE_PART_CHANCE) of randomly removing a body part during mutation, adding some genetic drift and variety to the evolving creatures. The existing mutation logic remains unchanged.\n\nThe evolve function in `evolution.gd` now also checks if a random float is less than MUTATION_RATE before replacing the current creature with the new one. This adds a small chance of keeping the current creature intact, which can help maintain some genetic diversity and prevent premature convergence on suboptimal solutions.", "wall_s": 12.02, "ts": "2026-07-03T13:37:39Z"}
{"worker": "forge", "role": "code_drafter", "model": "hermes3:8b", "model_requested": "codellama:13b", "fallback_skipped": ["codellama:13b", "qwen2.5-coder", "qwen2.5:7b", "iquest-coder-cpu:40b"], "task": "In 2 lines: any one small improvement you would ship to Wren's evolution loop today?", "reply": "# In `evolution.gd`:\n\nfunc _process(delta):\n    # Already checks for input and processes it\n    if Input.is_action_just_pressed(\"ui_accept\"):\n        evolve()\n\nfunc evolve():\n    # Evolve the creature based on fitness\n    var new_creature = creature.duplicate()\n    new_creature.mutate()\n    if new_creature.fitness > creature.fitness:\n        creature = new_creature\n\n# Patch:\n\nfunc evolve():\n    # Evolve the creature based on fitness\n    var new_creature = creature.duplicate()\n    new_creature.mutate()\n    if new_creature.fitness > creature.fitness:\n        creature = new_creature\n    print(\"Evolved to fitness:\", new_creature.fitness)  # Add this line\n\n# Explanation:\n\nThe small improvement is adding a simple `print` statement in the `evolve` function. This will output the current fitness of the evolved creature, allowing for easier monitoring and debugging of the evolution process.\n\nThis patch doesn't change the core functionality but provides useful feedback during development and testing.", "wall_s": 8.55, "ts": "2026-07-03T13:54:14Z"}
